# AA. PROOF AND ASSURANCE FRAMEWORK

## PM-PROOF-001 — Exact Proof World

A proof claim cannot splice green results from incompatible builds, kernels, Providers, policy/security generations, configs, or runs unless the claim explicitly permits composition.

## PM-PROOF-002 — Mandatory Dependency Axes

Each proof class defines mandatory dependency axes. Authors cannot omit dependencies merely to preserve PASS.

## PM-PROOF-003 — Claim Scope

Examples include `EXACT_HOST`, `HARDWARE_CLASS`, `BACKEND_VERSION`, `CONTRACT_ONLY`, `SECURITY_PROPERTY`, `PERFORMANCE_ENVELOPE`.

## PM-PROOF-004 — Preconditions

Proof claim lists required kernel features, memory floor, Provider trust tier, hardware capability, filesystem/storage mode, configuration, or other required environment.

## PM-PROOF-005 — Proof Identity/Integrity

Proof bundles are immutable/content-addressed and integrity-protected. Proof evidence may itself be disclosure-classified.

## PM-PROOF-006 — Proof Invalidation

Changing a mandatory dependency makes the old proof inapplicable to the changed body by default.

## PM-PROOF-007 — Reviewed Equivalence

Equivalence is a separate reviewed artifact. It does not rewrite the historical PASS and is not automatically transitive.

## PM-PROOF-008 — Reviewer/Evidence Independence

Evidence/reviewer relationship records `INDEPENDENT`, `NOT_INDEPENDENT`, or `UNKNOWN_INDEPENDENCE`. Different model/tool names do not automatically establish independence.

## PM-PROOF-009 — Mandatory Falsifier Frontier

Safety-relevant production-support claims derive required falsifier families/instances from frozen contracts. A named test is not proof the perturbation happened; a no-op perturbation does not count. Open fuzzing is empirical unless a bounded domain is actually exhausted.

## PM-PROOF-010 — Restraint Proof

Qualification includes safe controls proving that ordinary valid actions remain usable, redundant paths are not falsely protected, and unrelated optional-domain UNKNOWN does not globally disable the Host.

## PM-PROOF-011 — Bidirectional Proof-Subject Resolution

Run both:

```text
requirement → stable contract ID(s) → proof/fixture → expected PASS → claim scope
```

and:

```text
proof requirement → stable contract ID(s) → normative subject → expected PASS
```

An orphaned proof family is a regression finding.

## PM-PROOF-012 — Proof/Support Historical Key Rotation

Support/proof/evidence/audit signatures record algorithm/key epoch; key rotation preserves historical verification while old keys cannot issue new current authority.

