# AB. ROADMAP REVIEW GATES

## PM-GATE-DEF-001 — Definition Coverage

Every normative load-bearing concept has exactly one authoritative definition/reference and concept kind.

## PM-GATE-ID-001 — Stable-ID Coverage

Every normative contract and proof subject has a stable contract ID. Section-only proof subjects fail.

## PM-GATE-REG-001 — Contract Regression Diff

Every accepted contract from the immediate prior candidate and monotonic registry is accounted for. Silent deletion or silent semantic change blocks freeze.

## PM-GATE-MECH-001 — Authority-Mechanism Gate

Claims such as exclusive, fenced, non-occludable, durable-before-effect, rollback-resistant, revocation-bounded, control-isolated, or renderer-isolated must identify the enforcing mechanism class and proof obligation.

## PM-GATE-SM-001 — State-Machine Closure

Every stateful object defines creation, legal transitions, terminal/nonterminal states, idempotency, expiry, crash/restart, rollback compatibility, and retention/disposal where applicable.

## PM-GATE-PROOF-001 — Proof-Subject Resolution

Every proof requirement resolves to stable normative contracts and scoreable expected behavior, and every required product property resolves to a proof path.

## PM-GATE-PHASE-001 — Phase Feasibility

No phase requires proof or implementation that cannot yet exist. PM0 freezes foundational/PM1-required contracts and measurement methodology; implementation-dependent production envelopes are earned later.

## PM-GATE-DISTRESS-001 — Distress Gate

Production requires proof of the frozen minimum distress function set under CPU saturation, memory pressure, I/O pressure, process churn, service storm, Provider degradation, and audit/evidence pressure, without Manager outranking Core/Recovery/essential security/input authority.

## PM-GATE-INDEP-001 — Independent Falsification

After all internal gates are zero-defect for the same Review Input World, an independent reviewer attacks that exact world. Accepted corrections create a new Review Input World and require rerunning affected gates/review.

